 ],
 "literal": "Listen, may you live, friend! The lover / as cool drops of thread-broken pearls drip, / early in the morning grazing on the cool creeper of tāḷi, / on the very day when dew falls, departed. / The days of separation also will indeed become many.",
 "translation": "Listen, my friend, may you live long! Our lover departed on the very day when dew falls, when beasts graze early in the morning on the cool tāḷi creepers as cool drops like thread-broken pearls drip upon them. The days of his separation, too, will now become many.",
 "modern": "தோழியே, கேள்! நீ வாழ்க! நூல் அறுந்த முத்துக்களைப் போலக் குளிர்ந்த பனித்துளிகள் சிந்த, காலையிலேயே தாளி என்னும் குளிர்ந்த கொடியை விலங்குகள் மேய்கின்ற பனி பொழியும் காலத்தில்தான் நம் காதலர் நம்மைப் பிரிந்து சென்றார். அவர் பிரிந்திருக்கும் நாட்களும் இனிப் பலவாக நீளும் போலிருக்கிறது.",
 "explanation": "The heroine is speaking to her close friend about the pain of her lover's absence. She recalls the exact season of his departure, which was the cold, dewy season. The imagery of dew drops falling like pearls from a broken thread beautifully captures the fragile, cold atmosphere that mirrors her tears. Animals grazing on the cool tāḷi creepers early in the morning emphasizes the quiet, chilly dawn when he left. She laments that the days of this separation are stretching out and becoming too many to bear.",
